  "_about": "Software that documents name as their creator or producer (PDF /Creator and /Producer, XMP CreatorTool, OOXML Application and AppVersion), for the document collector (Unit 11). A metadata value matching one of a product's patterns (regular expressions, matched without case against the whole value from its start) is stored as that Product, and the File gets created_with to it, or to its ProductRelease when a version group captured one. A Product's unique_id is its CPE name as NVD's CPE dictionary writes it (cpe:2.3:part:vendor:product), so any collector that stores the same software converges on one Product; source shows NVD's dictionary entry. A ProductRelease is named \"<name> <version>\". vendor is the Organization stored as the Product's manufacturer. A value matching no product is kept as a property only. Add products here, not in Go code.",
